WEBVTT

00:55:27.000 --> 00:55:30.601
What he's found is that when people
think about passion as pleasure or joy,

00:55:30.625 --> 00:55:32.351
they're much less likely to succeed

00:55:32.375 --> 00:55:34.851
in pursuing whatever
they thought their passion was

00:55:34.875 --> 00:55:37.309
than if they think about it
as meaning and purpose.

00:55:37.333 --> 00:55:40.101
And I think that's because
emotions are much more fleeting

00:55:40.125 --> 00:55:42.934
and a sense of mattering
is much more sustainable.

00:55:42.958 --> 00:55:45.101
EP: It is very important,
what you just said.

00:55:45.125 --> 00:55:49.101
This is, I think passion
that is defined as joy and excitement --

00:55:49.125 --> 00:55:50.726
and what it does for me,

00:55:50.750 --> 00:55:54.143
is very different than passion
that is defined by the nature,

00:55:54.167 --> 00:55:56.809
the richness of the thing
in which you're plunging.

00:55:56.833 --> 00:56:00.684
You know, that is giving you meaning
because it is in itself meaningful.